{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Indeed, He loved the peoples.</b> He says: besides the fact that He gave them the Torah from His right hand from amidst the fire, He further loved them above all the peoples, for He called them סגולה, as it is said (Exodus 19:5): ״והייתם לי סגולה״ — and the Targum of סגולה is חביבין ('beloved'). Therefore he used חובב, which is the language of Targum, meaning that He loved them above all the peoples. Or: He loved them in that He called them עמים, as it is said: ״עמים הר יקראו״." "<b>And it is possible</b> to interpret: even at the time when He called them 'the people' (העם), which is a term of disgrace — in the manner of what is written (Numbers 25:1): ״ויחל העם״; (ibid. 21): ״וידבר העם״; (Exodus 32:25): ״ויקהל העם״; (ibid.): ״וירא משה את העם״ — behold, He loves them. Or one may say: אף חובב — even at the time of anger (אף), behold, He loves them, and His love does not depart from them. Why? Because they are His peoples, כל קדושיו בידך — all His holy ones are in Your hand, that is, all those consecrated in Israel, and they are the tribe of Levi, who surrendered themselves to death in Your hand; and this was in the sin of the calf, when all their kinsmen came and carried out Your will." "<b>And they trod (תכו).</b> They go and are drawn toward the place of the Ark, where ״הדום רגליך״ — the footstool of Your feet — is. And the word תכו is like הכו, for the tav is in place of the heh, in the language of (Hosea 11:3): ״תרגלתי לאפרים״, which is like הרגלתי; and likewise (Psalms 132:4): ״אם אתן שנת לעיני״; and likewise in Qohelet (8): ״עושה רע מאת״, where the tavs are in place of the hehs; and likewise we find a heh in place of a tav: ״ישימו קטורה״, which is like קטורת. And this, in my opinion, is from the secret of the language: for the heh is a sign of the feminine, such as אמרה, שמרה, קראה, and likewise for all verbs; therefore they placed it at the end. And there is in this an allusion to the final heh of the Name. And the tav too is a sign of the feminine for one speaking in the third person; therefore these two letters have one rule between them, since both of them indicate the feminine. And you already know that the final tav applies to all the letters." "<b>They bear Your utterances.</b> For they were the bearers of the Ark. Or one may say: ישא — each and every one of them bears Your utterances to Israel, because they were the teachers of the Torah, in the manner of what is written of the tribe of Levi: ״יורו משפטיך ליעקב״." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: תכו לרגלך — from the language of striking, for they are stricken on account of the holiness of the Shekhinah, which is ״הדום רגליך״ — the footstool of Your feet — which is bound to the Ark. And this alludes to the fact that the Ark would consume them, as the Sages of blessed memory mentioned; for this reason the tribe of Levi were few — their numbers did not rise to the tens of thousands but were fewer than all the tribes. And it says: ישא מדברותיך — for it is the vessel that bears the utterances, and from it we heard the Torah, in the manner of what Scripture says (Deuteronomy 5:4): ״מתוך האש״, and this is clear."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:54.835554077Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}